; AmiBroker ASCII import format for SYMBOL INFORMATION (name, alias, address, web, currency).
;
; Why $NOQUOTES 1: without it the importer demands a valid date and a non-zero price on every
; line, and a pure "metadata" file has neither. $NOQUOTES 1 switches off that validation, which
; is exactly what this file is for.
;
; Why $OVERWRITE 1: $AUTOADD alone would only touch symbols that do not exist yet. Every one of
; our 2,464 symbols already exists, so without OVERWRITE the whole file would parse, report
; success, and change nothing.
;
; Address is sanitised to a single line at export time (301 IDX addresses contain a newline, and
; a newline inside a CSV field splits one company into two malformed rows).
;
; Fundamental fields (EPS, BOOK_VALUE, MARKET_CAP, ...) are NOT imported even though the
; importer supports them: idx_fundamental stores 0 in every one of those columns for all 961
; symbols, and 0 is not a ratio - it is a missing value. Importing it would make AmiBroker
; report PER 0.00, which reads as "free" rather than "unknown".

$FORMAT Ticker,FullName,Alias,Address,WebID,Currency
$SEPARATOR ,
$SKIPLINES 0
$NOQUOTES 1
$OVERWRITE 1
$AUTOADD 1
$BREAKONERR 1
$DEBUG 1
